--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- chain on a sloping seabed (bathymetryFile) held by as-laid friction, surging fairlead, 60 s
-- The 410 m studless chain of chain_range_tdp.dat on a structured seabed instead of a flat one:
-- data/bathymetry/sloped_seabed.txt is a grid of `x y depth` rows, here a plane 60 m deep under
-- the fairlead that rises 2.1 deg toward the anchor (45 m deep at x = 400 m) and falls 2.9 deg
-- across the line, toward +Y. The seabed is bilinear between the grid points; bathymetryFile
-- replaces WtrDpth, which the deck must then leave out. Seabed friction (frictionMu 0.5) exceeds
-- the cross slope (tan 2.9 deg = 0.05), so the grounded chain holds; staticsFriction asLaid
-- solves the static start against the as-laid layout, the chain laid from the anchor along its
-- chord and its top end then moved to the fairlead, so the grounded length rests where it was
-- laid instead of sliding down the cross slope. The fairlead then surges 5 m at 30 s
-- (data/range_tdp/chain_surge_5m_30s_dt005.txt, after a 15 s smooth start). TDP1s and TDP1x
-- follow the touchdown point; L1N30py is the sideways position of a grounded node 290 m from
-- the fairlead, which friction keeps from creeping downslope.
